84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The Time Table Generator is a web-based application that creates a weekly class timetable from a set of subjects, teachers, rooms and available time slots. It is a college-level Data Structures and Algorithms \(DSA\) project built with Java and Spring Boot for the backend and HTML, CSS and JavaScript for the frontend. The system uses ArrayList to manage schedule entries and HashMap to track teacher, room and subject allocations. A greedy scheduling approach places activities into available slots while checking basic constraints such as teacher availability, room availability and duplicate assignments.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 57 0 R
/E (The browser sends the entered academic data to a Spring Boot REST endpoint. The backend validates the data, generates a timetable and returns the result as JSON. The frontend displays the timetable in a weekly grid and reports any activities that could not be scheduled. The first version uses user-entered sample data and does not require a database, login system or advanced optimization, keeping the project suitable for a college-level submission.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
